Nebula Browser
=============

[![ko-fi](https://ko-fi.com/img/githubbutton_sm.svg)](https://ko-fi.com/T1G020UH4L)

![Browsing on Apple TV](/screen01.png?raw=true "Nebula Browser on Apple TV")

![Tab overview](/screen02.png?raw=true "Nebula Browser tab overview")

![Settings menu](/screen03.png?raw=true "Nebula Browser settings menu")

![Full screen video player](/screen04.png?raw=true "Nebula Browser video player")


***Nebula Browser*** is a web browser for Apple TV devices running tvOS. It uses private API's that Apple normally does not allow in App Store distributed apps. Highlights:
- Uses WKWebView for fast, modern website rendering.
- Browser tabs with a focus-driven overview.
- Modern Liquid Glass UI with selectable accent themes (the app icon follows the theme).
- A built-in full screen video player with fast-forward, scrubbing and a transport bar.
- Multiple search engines, page zoom, and privacy options.

Nebula Browser was developed with the help of AI ([Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)): the full screen video player transport controls (fast-forward, scrubbing, transport bar, resume), the back/double-back navigation, the arrow button shortcuts, the per-page video fullscreen, the privacy options, and many input-handling fixes were built in collaboration with it. It is based on the open-source *tvOS Browser* by Steven Troughton-Smith and Jip van Akker.

This code is provided as is with no warranty or liability. Use at your own risk and do ***not*** distribute builds of this project on the App Store.


